              },
              "text" : "<span dir=\"ltr\" style=\"display: block;\">Dear {!$Expression.First_Name_1} {!$Expression.Last_Name_3},<br /><br />Zeta students have been having a busy school year! From the classrooms to the hallways, it has been a season of learning and a season of fun. <br /><br />Zeta Middle School is designed to help students enter high school academically prepared, increasingly independent, and confident in what they can accomplish.<br /><br />Students take demanding courses in English, history, math, and science. On <strong>the 2025-26 New York State Regents Exam, Zeta Middle School students earned a 97.5% pass rate in Algebra I and a 98.3% pass rate in Biology.</strong> New York students typically take these exams in high school! <br /><br />This kind of <strong>readiness also requires independence.</strong> Students meet with a trusted advisor who knows them deeply. During Advisory, they strengthen their self-knowledge, build financial literacy, and develop the skills to manage their time and advocate for themselves.<br /><br />In Z Lab, students identify real problems, design solutions, and test their ideas under real constraints. This work develops the Entrepreneurial Builder Mindset they will carry into high school, where they will build and pitch increasingly ambitious projects.<br /><br /></span>"
